items.answer_explanation:
将分子有理化，并将分母因式分解：
$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\sqrt{3-x}-\sqrt{1+x}}{x^2+x-2}
&=\frac{(3-x)-(1+x)}{(x^2+x-2)(\sqrt{3-x}+\sqrt{1+x})}\\
&=\frac{-2(x-1)}{(x-1)(x+2)(\sqrt{3-x}+\sqrt{1+x})}.
\end{aligned}
$$
当 $x\ne1$ 时约去 $x-1$，于是
$$
\begin{aligned}
\lim_{x\to1}\frac{\sqrt{3-x}-\sqrt{1+x}}{x^2+x-2}
&=\lim_{x\to1}\frac{-2}{(x+2)(\sqrt{3-x}+\sqrt{1+x})}\\
&=\frac{-2}{3\times2\sqrt2}\\
&=-\frac{\sqrt2}{6}.
\end{aligned}
$$

